  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1254 AM CDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\nBreezy southwest winds and lots of sunshine will result in near\nrecord to record high temperatures today through Tuesday. High\ntemperatures today will reach the upper 80s to around 90\ndegrees, with Tuesday a little warmer in the 88 to 95 degree\nrange. We may also see record warm overnight lows as readings \ntonight only drop into the 60s, and Tuesday night into the \nmiddle 60s to around 70 degrees. Temperatures will cool down a \nlittle for mid week, but will remain significantly above normal,\nespecially overnight lows.\n\nModels remain fairly consistent with the return of unsettled \nconditions for mid to late week.  A frontal boundary will sink into \nthe middle Mississippi and lower Ohio valleys Wednesday, meandering \nover our region into Thursday. A surface low will move along the \nfront Thursday into Thursday night, finally pushing the front on \nthrough our area.  The model blend still spreads chances of showers \nand thunderstorms across our region late Tuesday night into \nWednesday, continuing through Thursday night.  Friday is now dry, \nbut there are some model differences that bring down confidence that \nprecipitation will end by then, so some fine tuning is still likely. \nIn the meantime, precipitation chances are highest along and north \nof the front, and by Wednesday afternoon range from 30-60% across \nthe Pennyrile and Land Between the Lakes regions of west \nKentucky, to 70-95% across the rest of the PAH forecast area. \nThe pattern of lowest to highest chances from southeast to \nnorthwest will continue, with 30-65% chances Wednesday night, \n20-70% Thursday, and 10-40% Thursday night. \n\nBehind the frontal boundary Friday, windy conditions will \ndevelop with north to northwest winds at 15-25 mph with gusts \naround 30mph Friday into Friday evening. This will help usher in\nmuch cooler air, with highs Friday in the middle 60s to lower \n70s, and Saturday highs of 60 to 65 degrees. It will finally \nreally feel like fall with lows Friday night in the upper 30s to\nlower 40s, and Saturday night in the 35 to 40 degree range. A \nreturn of southerly winds Sunday will begin a warming trend, \nwith highs returning to around 70 degrees.",
